# Build context for `next build`. Everything here either cannot affect the
# build or must not reach the image. Docker matches these patterns per path
# component, so dot-directories are listed one by one rather than as `.*/`.

# Version control and CI
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.github

# Editor and agent tooling
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.claude
**/.agents
**/.cursor
**/.DS_Store
skills-lock.json

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/.next
out
build
coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Documentation and instructions
**/*.md

# Secrets. `.env.example` is excluded too: the image reads real environment
# variables, and shipping a template only invites confusion.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Local-only tooling
scripts
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/.pnpm-debug.log*
**/*.pem

# Docker's own files
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*
.dockerignore
